The 7 Layers of OSI – A Simple Breakdown 

📡 1. Physical Layer
 Wires, signals, connectors
 Like the delivery truck — it moves raw bits across cables or air.

🔗 2. Data Link Layer
 MAC addresses, switches
 Like the driver ensuring the package reaches the right apartment.

🗺️ 3. Network Layer
 IP addresses, routers
 Like the GPS deciding the best route across cities.

📦 4. Transport Layer
 TCP/UDP, ports
 Like handling and tracking the package — making sure it arrives safely and in order.

🚪 5. Session Layer
 Sessions, authentication
 Like ringing the doorbell and starting the delivery conversation.

🎁 6. Presentation Layer
 Encryption, encoding, formats
 Like unwrapping the box and translating the contents into a readable format.

🧑💻 7. Application Layer
 HTTP, SMTP, DNS
 Like opening the gift — the actual app
